ead":null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":-0.12725928911690787,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":0.0,"_gate_rev_durability":0.1022701280969407,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":76.1,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.025948246007761196,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":39.9,"_gate_share_shrink":0.03303519564316648,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":8.7,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.006157653395443627,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":89.7,"_gate_insider_own":0.00533,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":3.6,"_gate_insider_buying":1.0,"_gp_insider_buying":true,"_score_insider_buying":100.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Glacier Bancorp, Inc. operates as the bank holding company for Glacier Bank that provides commercial banking services to individuals, small to medium-sized businesses, community organizations, and public entities in the United States. It offers retail banking; business banking and mortgage origination and loan servicing services. The company also accepts deposit products, including non-interest bearing deposit and interest bearing deposit accounts, such as negotiable order of withdrawal, demand deposit accounts, savings, money market deposits, fixed rate certificates of deposit, negotiated-rate jumbo certificates, and individual retirement accounts. In addition, it offers credit risk management, construction and permanent loans on residential real estate, consumer land or lot loans, unimproved land and land development loans, construction loans, commercial real estate loans, agricultural and consumer lending, home equity loans, and states and political subdivisions lending, as well as residential builder guidance lines comprising pre-sold and spec-home construction, and lot acquisition loans. Glacier Bancorp, Inc. was founded in 1955 and is headquartered in Kalispell, Montana.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Randall M. Chesler | President, CEO & Director | Age 66 | Compensation: $2.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 4K people. Revenue per employee of $251K ranks in the bottom quartile among Financial Services peers, improving at 8%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $85K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 9\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Glacier Bancorp, Inc. is a mid-cap financial services business with a $6.3B market cap on $1.0B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +4% over the past three years and +10% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 8% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $348M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 34 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.57\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and thin 0.7\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 2.6% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 8.5% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 34% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","34 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Is Glacier Bancorp (GBCI) Undervalued After Its $200 Million Buyback And Strong Earnings?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/banks/nyse-gbci/glacier-bancorp/news/is-glacier-bancorp-gbci-undervalued-after-its-200-million-bu","date":"2026-11-03","timestamp":1793711878.332,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.898,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","dividend"]},{"title":"Share Buyback Plan Might Change The Case For Investing In Glacier Bancorp (GBCI)","source":"simplywall.st","link":